refused: d369_from_needs_a_growable_list.cy:9:55, line 9 column 55
 9 |     let $xs: std::coll::list<i32>[len.max: 4 items] = std::coll::list.from([1, 2], alloc: Lend $heap);
   |                                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 what: `std::coll::list.from` makes a list that grows on the heap, so it goes where one is written, with `len.max: inf items`
 why:  a list that grows on the heap is filled with `std::coll::list.from([1, 2, 3], alloc: Lend $heap)`, since every allocation names its allocator (D321, D369)
